# Rates, weather, and quotes

External data behind an explicit refresh. Run `wtf refresh` or use the
Refresh lookups lens; nothing is fetched while you type. Values are cached in
.wtf/lookups.json with their age, so notes keep working offline.

## Currencies

Money carries a currency: $, €, £, ¥ or a code after the number.

[€450]:hotel
[700 MXN]:cancellation_fee
[$1,200]:flights

[hotel_usd] := to(hotel, USD)
[fee_usd] := to(cancellation_fee, USD)
[eur_rate] := rate(EUR, USD)
[trip_total] := flights + hotel_usd + fee_usd

Hotel is [hotel] ([hotel_usd]); the trip totals [trip_total].

<!-- Different currencies never add up silently: hotel + flights is an error
until you convert one side with to(...). -->

## Weather

[oaxaca] := forecast("Oaxaca", 2026-11-20)
[oaxaca_f] := forecast("Oaxaca", 2026-11-20, F)
[packing_rain] := oaxaca.rain > 30%

Landing day looks like [oaxaca]; in Fahrenheit, [oaxaca_f].
Itinerary days with a place get a forecast in their inlay automatically:

## Friday, November 20, 2026 · New York | Oaxaca

07:04 AM  > Depart JFK for MEX

## Quotes

[shares] := 12
[nvda] := quote(NVDA) * shares

Holding [shares] shares is worth [nvda].

<!-- The built-in quote source is Yahoo's unofficial chart endpoint. Point
.wtf/providers.json at your own command to use something else:
{ "quote": "my-quote {symbol}" }  printing {"price": 42.5, "currency": "EUR"} -->
